    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352-a1">

                <pb facs="0639" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg507"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Appendix A—Extracts]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Draft Agreement on Treatment of Germany in the
                        Initial Control Period</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>9. Allied controls shall be imposed upon the German economy but only as may be
                    necessary:— <list>
                        <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>to carry out programmes, as prescribed by higher authority,<anchor
                                n="3" xml:id="d352-f1"/> of industrial disarmament and
                            demilitarisation, of reparations, of relief for liberated areas and of
                            other supplies as may be notified;</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <pb facs="0640" n="508" xml:id="pg508"/>
                <p>10. No action shall be taken in execution of the reparations programme or
                    otherwise which would tend to support basic living standards in Germany on a
                    higher level than that existing in any one of the neighboring United
                        Nations.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d352-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>11. The first charge on all approved exports for reparations or otherwise shall
                    be a sum necessary to pay for approved imports.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d352-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>12. Recurrent reparations should not by their form or amount require the
                    rehabilitation or development of German heavy industry and should not foster the
                    dependence of other countries upon the German economy.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d352-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d352-f1" n="3" xml:id="d352-f1-content">
                <p>The words “as prescribed by higher authority” have been stricken from the draft
                    in Byrnes’ and Matthews’ copies of the Briefing Book.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d352-f2" n="4" xml:id="d352-f2-content">
                <p>The following manuscript notation appears in the margin of Byrnes’ copy of the
                    Briefing Book opposite this paragraph: “out”. In Matthews’ copy this paragraph
                    has been stricken from the draft.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d352-f3" n="5" xml:id="d352-f3-content">
                <p>In Matthews’ copy this paragraph has been marked to be stricken from the
                    draft.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d352-f4" n="6" xml:id="d352-f4-content">
                <p>In Matthews’ copy this paragraph has been stricken from the draft and the
                    following manuscript substitute written in the margin: “12. The principles
                    governing the exaction of reparations from Germany are set forth in Annex <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">i</hi> to this agreement.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
